      en: "The Royal BC Museum in Victoria is a premier institution dedicated to preserving and sharing British Columbia's human and natural history. Founded in 1886, the museum houses over 7 million specimens and artifacts. Its permanent galleries include the First Peoples Gallery, the Modern History Gallery, and the Natural History Gallery, featuring a replica of a coastal temperate rainforest and a full-size woolly mammoth. The museum also has an IMAX theatre and conducts research expeditions. It attracts around 800,000 visitors annually and is a key cultural attraction in Victoria.",
