      en: "Château Ramezay is a historic mansion in Montreal, built in 1705 as the residence of Claude de Ramezay, governor of Montreal. It is one of the oldest buildings in the city and has served various roles, including a residence, the headquarters of the American Revolutionary forces in 1775-76, and a museum since 1894. The building features period rooms and exhibits on Quebec's history. It is a National Historic Site of Canada and houses an extensive collection of artifacts related to the French and English colonial periods, including the original 1705 deed of the property.",
