      en: "Fort Malden, located in Amherstburg, Ontario, was built by the British Army in 1795 to defend the border with the United States. During the War of 1812, it served as a key base for British forces and their Indigenous allies. After the war, the fort fell into disrepair but was later restored. It is now a National Historic Site of Canada. The fort features several faithfully reconstructed buildings, including the officers' quarters and guardhouse. Visitors can explore the region's military history through interactive exhibits and demonstrations. The site offers scenic views of the Detroit River.",
