      en: "The Britannia Mine Museum in Britannia Beach, British Columbia, is located on the site of the former Britannia copper mine. The mine operated from 1904 to 1974 and was one of the largest copper mines in the British Empire. The museum offers underground tours through the tunnels, showcasing miners' working conditions. Exhibits include original machinery, tools, and a functioning ore mill. The site is a protected heritage property and provides insight into the region's mining history. Visitors can also try gold panning.",
